direction(5,'The tentative inseparable degree two after Veronese',4,4,[29,78,92],[13,19,58],'A precise scope for the degree-two assertion, or a counterexample in the remaining intended scope.','The conic gives degree2; SGA7 distinguishes ordinary tangency from separable duality; arbitrary original Gauss maps have broader behavior.','First determine whether the source sentence refers to the original embedding or to a sufficiently ample Veronese, then compare the local ordinary-tangency extension.')
direction(6,'Global irreducibility from the proposed incidence axioms',5,2,[54,55],[37,38],'Either an exact global Bertini theorem from the listed axioms or a missing primitive axiom/counterexample.','The local transversality dimension proof works; later axiomatic papers were located but their exact equivalence was not verified.','Write the full axiom list without commentary, test the generic fiber’s geometric connectedness, and obtain the restricted later full texts before claiming novelty.')
